<!-- #region q2 -->

**Step 1. Predict with the starting values** $w_0 = 0,\ b_0 = 0$, so every $\hat y_i = 0$.

| i | $x_i$ | $y_i$ | $\hat y_i = wx_i + b$ | $y_i - \hat y_i$ | $x_i(y_i - \hat y_i)$ |
|:-:|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|--:|
| 1 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 2 | 2 |
| 2 | 2 | 4 | 0 | 4 | 8 |
| 3 | 3 | 6 | 0 | 6 | 18 |
| **Σ** |  |  |  | **12** | **28** |

**Step 2. The gradients** (formulas given in the question):

$$ \begin{aligned} \frac{\partial J}{\partial w} &= -\frac{2}{n}\sum x_i\,(y_i - \hat y_i) = -\frac{2}{3}(28) = -18.6667 \\ \frac{\partial J}{\partial b} &= -\frac{2}{n}\sum (y_i - \hat y_i) = -\frac{2}{3}(12) = -8 \end{aligned} $$

**Step 3. Update both from the old values** (move against the gradient):

$$ \begin{aligned} w_1 &= w_0 - \eta\,\frac{\partial J}{\partial w} = 0 - 0.1\,(-18.6667) = \mathbf{1.8667} \\ b_1 &= b_0 - \eta\,\frac{\partial J}{\partial b} = 0 - 0.1\,(-8) = \mathbf{0.8} \end{aligned} $$

**Check that it worked.** The cost before the step is $J(0, 0) = \frac{1}{3}(2^2 + 4^2 + 6^2) = 18.6667$. After it, the predictions are 2.6667, 4.5333, 6.4, so $J(1.8667, 0.8) = 0.2963$. The cost fell, so the step went the right way.

<!-- #endregion q2 -->
<!-- #region q3 -->

There are **3 positives** (S1, S3, S5) and **3 negatives** (S2, S4, S6). At threshold t, predict positive when the probability is **≥ t**.

| Threshold | Called positive | TP | FP | FN | TN | TPR = TP/(TP+FN) | FPR = FP/(FP+TN) |
|:-:|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|--:|--:|
| 0.9 | S1 | 1 | 0 | 2 | 3 | 1/3 = 0.333 | 0/3 = 0 |
| 0.8 | S1, S2 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1/3 = 0.333 | 1/3 = 0.333 |
| 0.7 | S1, S2, S3 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 2/3 = 0.667 | 1/3 = 0.333 |
| 0.6 | S1, S2, S3, S4 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 2/3 = 0.667 | 2/3 = 0.667 |
| 0.4 | S1, S2, S3, S4, S5 | 3 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 3/3 = 1 | 2/3 = 0.667 |
| 0.3 | S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S6 | 3 | 3 | 0 | 0 | 3/3 = 1 | 3/3 = 1 |

**The ROC points**, adding (0, 0) for a threshold above every score: (0, 0), (0, 0.333), (0.333, 0.333), (0.333, 0.667), (0.667, 0.667), (0.667, 1), (1, 1).

